Tagaraśikhi(n), (Pali ˚sikhi, a Paccekabuddha),
(1) n. of a former Buddha: ˚khiṃ, acc., and ˚khir, n., Mv 〔iii.233.7〕 (prose); read Tagāra˚ with best ms. (ā m.c.) LV 〔172.12〕 (vs);
(2) n. of a pratyekabuddha: ˚khī Karmav 〔57.18〕; 〔58.1〕; 〔68.9〕; 〔70.2〕. Is (1) really the same as (2) ? Hardly in Mv, where he is predicted by an earlier Buddha and predicts the next one.
